# agent-rules Module Refactor — Implementation Status

Date: 2026-07-14
Branch: feat/checkout-journey-both-channels

## Completed Fixes (5 of 5 proposed HIGH/MEDIUM items)

### HIGH Fixes

- **[DONE] H1**: Fix optional checkout-settings dependency (GetAgentContextUseCase)
  - File: `application/agent-rules.use-cases.ts` (lines 64–72)
  - Removed `@Optional()` decorator; adapter is now required
  - Renamed `withCheckoutContext` to `enrichWithCheckoutContext` for clarity
  - Updated all tests to provide noop adapter (side-effect-free)
  - Impact: Silent degradation eliminated; failures are explicit

- **[DONE] H2**: Strengthen DTO Patch Validation
  - File: `presentation/http/dto/agent-rules-patch.dto.ts` (complete rewrite)
  - Added cross-field validation: `hasAnySection()` rejects empty patches
  - Added bounds on array sizes: blockedPhrases (200), requiredDisclaimers (50), etc.
  - Added runtime guard: safety toggles (forbidUnauthorizedDiscounts, forbidUnauthorizedFreeShipping) now default to `true` only (DTO enforces)
  - Added `@IsNotEmpty()` on agentName, `@ValidateIf()` on greeting
  - Impact: Invalid patches rejected at HTTP 400 level

- **[DONE] H3**: Type-safe request extraction in controller
  - File: `presentation/http/agent-rules.controller.ts` (lines 9–17, all routes)
  - Removed `as { user?: unknown }` cast; defined `AuthenticatedRequest` interface
  - `currentUser(request)` throws UnauthorizedException if user missing (guard already enforces)
  - Impact: Type safety; no `as` casts; clear contract

### MEDIUM Fixes

- **[DONE] M1**: Extract JSON converters to separate file
  - File: `infrastructure/prisma-agent-rules.converters.ts` (new)
  - Extracted `toCreate`, `toUpdate`, `toAgentRules` as explicit functions
  - Impact: Converters now testable; visible data transformations

- **[DONE] M2**: Module exports more use-cases
  - File: `agent-rules.module.ts` (line 32)
  - Changed from `exports: [GetAgentContextUseCase]` to `exports: [GetAgentRulesUseCase, UpdateAgentRulesUseCase, GetAgentContextUseCase]`
  - Impact: Other modules can now compose any use-case

- **[DONE] M3**: E2E test validates DTO path
  - File: `presentation/http/agent-rules.prisma-e2e-spec.ts` (lines 59–61)
  - Added explicit `AgentRulesPatchDto` type annotation
  - E2E now calls controller (which runs ValidationPipe) instead of use-case directly
  - Impact: DTO validation path exercised in E2E

